Problem Statement
AI-Agent-Powered Caregiver Intelligence & Dementia Support

Dementia patients often face:

Memory loss and repeated questioning
Disorientation and confusion
Anxiety and emotional distress
Difficulty remembering people, routines and important events
Continuous dependence on caregivers

At the same time, caregivers cannot monitor and support the patient 24/7.

Our Solution — WECARE

A memory-safe, voice-first AI companion that supports dementia patients while keeping caregivers informed and in control.

Core idea

Patient → AI Companion → Caregiver → Human Intervention

Personalized Verified Memory Architecture
Voice-based AI interaction
Safe, policy-controlled responses
Distress/risk signal detection
Real-time caregiver alerts
Guardian monitoring & memory approval

SLIDE 2 — WHY THIS SOLUTION?
Why WECARE?
❌ Problem with existing generic AI

A normal LLM may:

Invent personal information
Give contradictory answers
Trigger confusion
Discuss sensitive topics without context
✅ Our approach

1. Personalized

AI responds using the patient's verified life history.

2. Memory-Safe

AI cannot freely invent personal facts.

3. Stage-Aware

Responses can be adapted to the patient's cognitive/communication needs.

4. Human-in-the-Loop

Caregivers remain the final decision-makers.

5. Context-Aware Alerts

Not every unusual event becomes an emergency alert.

⭐ Key Differentiator

“Existing systems track events. WECARE understands the context behind them.”

The project specifically uses verified memories, caregiver approval, sensitive-topic controls and controlled response strategies rather than unrestricted conversation.

